  "comment": "14 regions: crown, west_shoulder, 3 district pads (Urban/Recife/HIVEMIND), harbor_bay, and a 9-cell woodlands grid. Content lives in host-owned EchoRegion containers built/evicted through WorldStreamer::setRegionHooks (echo_regions.h, WP-1) \u2014 this graph runs the residency ENGINE only (wants/budget/hysteresis/proxy); no region here carries a Scene-ledger `leveldoc` OR a real ledger `builder` (Lane A is intentionally empty in Echotropolis, plan \u00a70). world_stream.cpp:77-80 hard-requires a non-empty `builder` or `leveldoc` to pass load() validation, so every region below carries a `builder` of the form `echoregion:<id>` \u2014 a value NOT in world_stream.cpp:266-274's whitelist (\"city\"|\"oceanbase\"|\"worldregions\"), so WorldStreamer::realize() logs one harmless '[worldstream] region `<id>`: unknown builder' line per (re)build before falling through to the region hooks (m_onRegionBuild, called unconditionally right after the ledger dispatch \u2014 world_stream.cpp:279) that actually build the content. This is the documented minimal-valid shape for a hook-only region under the CURRENT loader; it is not a functional bug, just log noise, and is flagged for WP-0/whoever touches world_stream.cpp next as a candidate for a real 'hookonly'/'none' sentinel in the whitelist. anchor=[x,y,z] world metres (y is NOT used by residency math \u2014 WorldStreamer::distToFootprint only reads x/z \u2014 so district/woodlands y values are nominal, not runtime-authoritative; runtime code should still sample hf.heightAt(anchor) for real placement per the plan's elevation note). radius = authored footprint (XZ) edge; loadRadius/unloadRadius = hysteresis measured from that edge (load closer than loadRadius, unload only past unloadRadius). Neighbors are listed symmetrically (matching regions.json/regions.canon.json's existing convention) and get a 1.5x load-radius warm automatically (plan \u00a71).",
